    Never calls the provider. A staged 200 result is the durable fact: append
    the single success event (deduplicated on event_id), mark the mirror
    committed and return the stored envelope. Without a durable result the
    in-memory envelope cannot be recovered and the backend must not be
    re-invoked, so the attempt stays pending (the mirror stays its evidence)
    and the caller answers a retryable strand fault.
